WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.082 --> 00:00:01.250
(adventurous music)

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.930
- I've been called a rock star botanist,

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.210
because I do roping,
cliff climbing, hiking

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.830
miles and miles and miles, but

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.850
that was where the plants were.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.010
There is this huge extinction crisis

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.730
going on in Hawaii, and my caring

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.582
about the plants is
really what is driving me.

00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:20.717
(adventurous music)
(helicopter whirring)

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:22.050
Everything OK?

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.140
Well my name is Steve
Perlman, and I do work

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.520
for the plant extinction
prevention program in Hawaii.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.810
Our program focuses on the plants

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.600
that are extremely rare in Hawaii,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.768
that have less than 50
individuals left in the wild.

00:00:38.768 --> 00:00:41.580
(gentle music)

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.390
This is a crater of Mount Wai'ale'ale,

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.330
the rainiest spot on earth, and then

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:49.560
in this special spot, there
are several species of plants

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.840
that are only known from
this area and nowhere else.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.060
(lighthearted music)

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.090
What we'll do, is try
to make seed collections

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:02.140
of these really rare species
that are going extinct.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.300
This is the cyanea asarifolia,
they're extremely rare.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.440
I'm bagging the immature fruit right here,

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.690
so that we can come back
and get seeds later.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.730
Field botanists these
days are really having

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.590
to push the limits to get
to a lot of our plants.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.100
The rocks are slippery,
it's sometimes muddy,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.710
and very steep, there are no trails,

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.270
people rarely come back here.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.150
This is the lysimachia iniki, nowhere else

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.470
in the world does this thing grow.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.660
About 40 plants or so
are known, and that's it.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.690
And we only can get it when it washes down

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.794
the cliffs in heavy rains and storms.

00:01:41.794 --> 00:01:44.461
(ambient music)

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.010
There is a wonderful feeling, to go into

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:52.500
these remote areas and then
successfully locate plants.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.270
This plant is beautiful and unique,

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.094
they've evolved in the Hawaiian islands.

00:01:59.094 --> 00:02:00.190
(relaxed music)

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.060
You're out there with a plant that has

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.030
only one or two of the
plants left in the wild,

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.700
you're really, really feeling the emotion

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.840
of what that's like, you
go and visit those plants

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.880
many times, it's often
becomes like your family.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.920
It has been a really strenuous career,

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.590
I'm turning 70 years old next month,

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.350
and I still love the work that I do.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.620
I think I'd probably be bored just hanging

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.940
around the house, and I don't like

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.720
to watch much TV or things like that,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.335
so I wanna keep doing
this work and not retire.

00:02:31.335 --> 00:02:34.418
(lighthearted music)

